# Copy to supabase/.env and fill in. Read by the Supabase CLI, not by Next.js —
# it resolves every env(...) reference in config.toml from here.
#
# The CLI looks for dotenv files in supabase/ first, then the project root, and the
# ambient shell environment beats both. supabase/.env is already gitignored by the
# root .gitignore's `.env*` rule.

# The Google OAuth client — the same one production uses.
#
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → your Web application client.
# Add http://127.0.0.1:54421/auth/v1/callback to its Authorized redirect URIs, alongside
# the production https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback. That address is the
# local GoTrue container, which is why it is port 54421 and not the app's 3000.
#
# Nothing about this weakens production: the OAuth client is allowed to redirect to both,
# and which one it uses is decided by whichever Supabase issued the request.
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET=
